From 01fbb8b0e8af80c9023ed0ca4602c8875ad00ffa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:35:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: send two spatial streams on HT-PHY

HT-PHY devices advertise and receive MCS 8-15, but send one spatial
stream only, as sending two with the three HT-PHY cores had not been
tested. The default antenna setting puts cores 0 and 1 in the PHY TX
control word, which is what MCS 8-15 need.

Let HT-PHY devices send two streams, as N-PHY devices do.

On a BCM4331 (HT-PHY rev 1, chain masks 7) on 5 GHz at -52 dBm,
against iperf3 on the access point, minstrel moves from MCS 7 with the
short guard interval to MCS 13-15, and the upload goes from 42-43 to
50-58 Mbit/s in 10 s runs, and to 46 Mbit/s in a 60 s run. The
download stays at 72-78 Mbit/s.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -5765,9 +5765,6 @@ static void b43_ht_cap_set_chains(struct
 	int rx = hweight8(sprom->rxchain & mask) ?: cores;
 	int tx_ss = min(tx, 2), rx_ss = min(rx, 2);
 
-	/* Sending two streams has not been tested with the three HT-PHY cores */
-	if (dev->phy.type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
-		tx_ss = 1;
 	if (rx_ss >= 2)
 		ht_cap->mcs.rx_mask[1] = 0xff;
 	if (tx < 2)
